            <ArticleTitle>[Hyperprolactinemia associated with acute intermittent porphyria].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>601-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Galactorrhea as the result of hyperprolactinemia has been described in very rare cases associated to acute outbreaks of intermittent acute porphyria (IAP). In our country, any of such cases have been published or analytically documented. We present the case of a patient admitted in our hospital for the study of abdominal pain and galactorrhea, with latter diagnosis of IAP, supported by the assessment of the activity of the enzyme showing a deficit in the red blood cells.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
